# UC02 — ESG / Sustainability Audit

**Mode**: Repeat (same questions × N companies → comparison table)
**Persona**: Sustainability lead prepping CSRD, or auditor verifying ESG disclosures
**Scenario**: 15 distinct ESG questions asked verbatim of each company's annual/sustainability report. Output is a comparison table showing how each company answers each question.

## Files in this folder

- [corpus.md](artifact:?) — source documents with provenance
- [questions-and-answers.md](artifact:?) — 15 questions × 2 companies = 30 ground-truth cells
- [`data-sources/`](artifact:?) — the actual report files

## Status

- Vertical-slice scope: 2 companies (H&M Group + Ørsted). Defers Unilever (Akamai-blocked direct download) and CSRD/ESRS framework as a separate reference doc to v2.
- Source docs: 2 of 2 ready, SHA-256s captured
- Questions: 15 drafted
- Ground truth: 30 cells drafted (single human pass; needs second-human review)
- Outstanding: second-human review pass; v2 corpus expansion (Unilever via mirror, ESRS framework reference)

## Summary metrics

- **Question types**: 8 numerical extraction · 4 classification (framework/assurance/Yes-No) · 2 reasoning · 1 trap
- **Industry contrast**: H&M (fast fashion, high Scope 3 burden) vs Ørsted (offshore wind, renewable producer). Same questions surface very different answer shapes — strong test of competitor's ability to map each company's reporting style.
- **Reporting maturity contrast**: H&M (transitioning to CSRD, TCFD+GRI based) vs Ørsted (first fully CSRD/ESRS-compliant 2024 report). Tests competitor's understanding of framework alignment.

